<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Connectly — Saved Posts</title>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- ===== Navbar ===== -->
    {{>header}}

    <!-- ===== Saved Posts Page ===== -->
    <main class="saved-page">
      <div class="saved-container">
        <div class="page-header">
          <h1>Saved Posts</h1>
          <p>Posts you've bookmarked for later reading.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Filter Tabs -->
        <div class="filter-tabs" id="savedFilters">
          <button
            class="filter-tab active"
            data-filter="all"
            type="button"
          >All</button>
          <button
            class="filter-tab"
            data-filter="design"
            type="button"
          >Design</button>
          <button
            class="filter-tab"
            data-filter="travel"
            type="button"
          >Travel</button>
          <button
            class="filter-tab"
            data-filter="tech"
            type="button"
          >Technology</button>
          <button
            class="filter-tab"
            data-filter="food"
            type="button"
          >Food</button>
        </div>

        <!-- Saved Posts List -->
        <div class="saved-posts-grid" id="savedPostsGrid">
          <!-- Saved Post 1 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="design">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar">AS</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Alex Silva</a>
                <span class="post-username">@alexsilva</span>
                <span class="post-time">2 hours ago</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Design</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>My top 5 design principles for building products people love:
                1. Clarity over cleverness 2. Consistency builds trust 3.
                Feedback at every step 4. Accessibility is not Optional 5. Less,
                but better.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 24 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span> 8 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Saved Post 2 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="travel">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar post-avatar-2">MK</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Maya Kapoor</a>
                <span class="post-username">@mayakapoor</span>
                <span class="post-time">5 hours ago</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Travel</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>10 lessons from 10 years of hiking. #1: The best views come
                after the hardest climbs. Nature has a way of putting everything
                into perspective. Here's my complete guide to planning your
                first multi-day trek.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 56 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span>
                15 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Saved Post 3 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="tech">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar post-avatar-3">JT</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Jordan Tate</a>
                <span class="post-username">@jordantate</span>
                <span class="post-time">Yesterday</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Technology</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>I just migrated my entire portfolio from a traditional CMS to a
                headless setup with static generation. Page load times dropped
                from 3.2s to 0.4s. Here's the full breakdown of what I learned.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 112 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span>
                32 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Saved Post 4 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="food">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar post-avatar-4">RL</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Riley Lee</a>
                <span class="post-username">@rileylee</span>
                <span class="post-time">2 days ago</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Food</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>After 6 months of experimenting with pour-over coffee, I've
                finally found the perfect ratio: 1:16 coffee to water, 30 second
                bloom, total brew time 3 minutes. Game changer. Here's my full
                setup and technique guide.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 38 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span>
                21 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Saved Post 5 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="design">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar post-avatar-2">MK</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Maya Kapoor</a>
                <span class="post-username">@mayakapoor</span>
                <span class="post-time">3 days ago</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Design</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>The best color palettes don't just look good — they
                communicate. I analyzed 50 award-winning websites and found that
                80% use a maximum of 3 primary colors. Here's my full analysis
                with swatches and takeaways.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 89 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span>
                17 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>

          <!-- Saved Post 6 -->
          <article class="post-card saved-post-card" data-category="tech">
            <div class="post-header">
              <div class="post-avatar">AS</div>
              <div class="post-meta">
                <a href="profile.html" class="post-author">Alex Silva</a>
                <span class="post-username">@alexsilva</span>
                <span class="post-time">5 days ago</span>
              </div>
              <span class="saved-tag">Technology</span>
            </div>
            <div class="post-content">
              <p>Stop building your own auth system. Seriously. Use established
                providers, focus on your product. I made this mistake on three
                projects before learning. Here's why auth is the last thing you
                should roll your own solution for.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="post-actions">
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#10084;</span> 167 Likes</span>
              <span class="post-action"><span>&#128172;</span>
                44 Comments</span>
              <button class="post-action js-remove-save" type="button">
                <span>&#128278;</span>
                Remove Bookmark
              </button>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>

        <!-- Empty State (hidden by default, shown when all posts removed) -->
        <div class="empty-state hidden" id="emptyState">
          <div class="empty-icon">&#128218;</div>
          <h2>No Saved Posts Yet</h2>
          <p>When you bookmark posts from your feed, they'll appear here for
            easy access later.</p>
          <a href="feed.html" class="btn-primary">Browse Feed</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <!-- ===== Footer ===== -->
    {{>footer}}

    <script type="module" src="js/main.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>